[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Power Management
REQ_PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-13-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: System Power States

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-4
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Multiple system power states
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall define a set of system power states that differ in power
consumption and wake-up latency.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-15
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Active state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall define an active state in which the system is fully powered
and operational.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-16
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Runtime idle state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall define a runtime idle state in which the CPUs enter their
deepest idle state and wait for interrupts, while devices remain in their current
states.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-17
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Suspend-to-idle state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall define a suspend-to-idle state in which the CPUs enter their
deepest idle state and peripherals may be placed into low-power states, without
loss of CPU execution context.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-18
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Standby state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall define a standby state in which peripherals are placed into
low-power states and all non-boot CPUs are powered off.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-19
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Suspend-to-RAM state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall define a suspend-to-RAM state in which the system is powered
off except for the memory, which retains the saved state of the CPUs and devices.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-20
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Suspend-to-disk state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall define a suspend-to-disk state in which the system, including
the memory, is powered off, with the memory contents saved to non-volatile storage
and restored on resume.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-21
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Soft-off state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall define a soft-off state in which no system state is preserved
and from which the system resumes by restarting as from initial power-up.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: System Power Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-1
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Power State Control
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide control over changes to system power states.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-5
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Entering a low-power state when idle
STATEMENT: >>>
When all CPUs become idle, the Zephyr RTOS shall place the system into a low-power
state selected by the power management policy.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Overriding the policy with a specified state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to bypass the power management policy and
place the system into a specified power state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-22
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Application-defined power management policy
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support replacing the default power management policy with an
application-defined policy that selects the system power state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Power Management Policy

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-6
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Power state selection by anticipated idle time
STATEMENT: >>>
Where the default power management policy is used, the Zephyr RTOS shall select the
system power state based on the time remaining until the next scheduled kernel
event.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Preventing entry into a power state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to prevent the system from entering a
specified power state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-23
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Allowing entry into a power state again
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to lift a previously imposed restriction
on entering a specified power state, allowing entry into the state again once all
such restrictions have been lifted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-24
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Querying whether a power state is prevented
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to query whether entry into a specified
power state is currently prevented.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Wake-up latency constraint
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to impose a maximum wake-up latency
constraint on system power state selection.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-25
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Wake-up latency constraint enforcement
STATEMENT: >>>
While a wake-up latency constraint is active, the Zephyr RTOS shall not enter a
system power state whose wake-up latency exceeds the constraint.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-26
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Updating a wake-up latency constraint
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to update the value of an active wake-up
latency constraint.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-27
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Removing a wake-up latency constraint
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to remove a previously imposed wake-up
latency constraint.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-28
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Notification of wake-up latency constraint changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to be notified when the effective wake-up
latency constraint changes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Power State Notifications

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-3
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Notification of changes to system power states
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide notification of changes to system power states.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
When the power state is changed I want to get a notification so that specific parts of my application can react accordingly.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-29
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Registering a power state notifier
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to register a notifier for system power
state transitions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-30
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Unregistering a power state notifier
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to unregister a previously registered
power state notifier.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-31
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Power state entry notification
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system enters a power state, the Zephyr RTOS shall invoke the state entry
callback of each registered notifier with the state being entered.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-32
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Power state exit notification
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system exits a power state, the Zephyr RTOS shall invoke the state exit
callback of each registered notifier with the state being exited.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Device Power Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Device power states
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support device power states, including active, suspended, and
off, and a transitional suspending state for devices that suspend asynchronously.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Device power state transitions
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to request a device to transition between
its power states.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-33
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Unsupported device power state transition
STATEMENT: >>>
If a requested device power state transition is not supported by the device, then
the Zephyr RTOS shall return an error indicating the operation is not supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-34
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Device already in requested power state
STATEMENT: >>>
If a device is already in the power state implied by a requested transition, then
the Zephyr RTOS shall return an error indicating the device is already in that
state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-35
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Device busy during power state transition
STATEMENT: >>>
If a device power state transition is requested while the device is changing its
power state, then the Zephyr RTOS shall return an error indicating the device is
busy.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-13
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Querying device power state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to query the current power state of a
device.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Runtime Device Power Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-36
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Enabling runtime power management for a device
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to enable runtime power management for a
device.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-37
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Disabling runtime power management for a device
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to disable runtime power management for a
device.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Resuming a device on use
STATEMENT: >>>
When a device managed by runtime power management is claimed by its first user, the
Zephyr RTOS shall resume the device.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-38
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Suspending an unused device
STATEMENT: >>>
When the last user of a device managed by runtime power management releases the
device, the Zephyr RTOS shall suspend the device.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-39
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Asynchronous device release
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to release a device managed by runtime
power management asynchronously, suspending it only after a specified delay has
elapsed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: CPU Idle

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-14
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Idling the current CPU
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to place the current CPU into a
low-power idle state until an interrupt occurs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-13-40
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Idling the current CPU with atomic interrupt enable
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to place the current CPU into a
low-power idle state, atomically re-enabling interrupts as the CPU enters the idle
state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-10

[[/SECTION]]
